(4)
Initiate investigations for the purpose of discovering violations of this chapter;
(5)
Conduct hearings upon charges calling for the discipline of a licensee or on violations of this chapter;
(6)
Conduct national background checks by the submission of fingerprints to the Federal Bureau of Investigation through the Georgia Crime Information Center;
(7)
Adopt a seal;
(8)
Establish rules and regulations relating to ethical conduct of persons licensed and regulated pursuant to this chapter; and
(9)
Do all other things necessary to administer and enforce this chapter and all rules and regulations adopted by the board pursuant to this chapter.
